<%args>
	$err => undef
</%args>
<%init>

</%init>

	<script>
		<!--function sf(){document.f.email.focus();} -->
	</script>

	<div class="main">

		<div class="centeralign">
		<span class="ninetenths leftalign">

		<h2>Password Reset</h2>

		<p class="bluebordertop martopmore">
		</p>

		<p>
			Hey, it happens.  The summertime is long, you lost track and..you
			forgot your password.  I'm here to help.
		</p>

		<p class="bluetext">
			So, enter the email address connected to your Tabroom.com account
			in the box below, and we'll get your password reset.
		</p>

		<form
			action = "forgot_send.mhtml"
			method = "post"
		>
			<input
				type  = "hidden"
				name  = "origin_ip"
				value = "<% $ENV{HTTP_X_FORWARDED_FOR} %>"
			>

			<div class="row centeralign">
				<span class="third semibold">
					Your Tabroom Email Address
				</span>

				<span class="twothirds">
					<input
						type        = "text"
						name        = "username"
						placeholder = "Enter email"
					>
				</span>
			</div>

			<div class="liblrow rightalign">
				<span class="third centeralign">
					<input
						name  ="submit"
						class ="greentext"
						type  ="submit"
						value ="I Have A Code"
					>
				</span>
				<span class="third centeralign">
				</span>
				<span class="third centeralign">
					<input
						type  ="submit"
						name  ="submit"
						value ="Send Reset Code"
					>
				</span>
			</div>

		</form>

		</span>
		</div>
	</div>

	<div class="menu">
		<div class="sidenote">

			<h5>Some things to remember...</h5>

			<p class="bigger">
				Your tabroom.com login is tied to the email address you used
				when you first created it.  If you have changed your email
				address, try logging in with the old email address as your
				username. You can do so even if you don't have access to that
				old email!
			</p>

			<p class="bigger">
				You can change your email address or password within
				tabroom.com by clicking the person-icon in the top right corner
				of the screen after you log in.
			</p>

			<p class="bigger">
				Your password is case sensitive; be sure if you capitalized
				anything when you created it, you must do so to log in.
				However, emails are not case sensitive; upper and lower case do
				not matter.
			</p>

			<p class="bigger">
				Cookies must be enabled on your browser for Tabroom.com to work,
				as must Javascript.
			</p>

			<p class="bigger">
				If you cannot remember your password, or no longer have access
				to your original email to get a reminder, or do not remember
				your email address, please email us at <% $Tab::admin_email %>.
			</p>

		</div>
	</div>
